<title>GREECE: GREECE RAISES 400BLN DRS FROM SECURITIES - BANKERS.</title>
<headline>GREECE RAISES 400BLN DRS FROM SECURITIES - BANKERS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek bankers said that the finance ministry raised about 400 billion drachmas from the sale of 12-month T-bills and two-year zero coupon bonds on sale today.</p>
<p>The 12-month T-bill featuring a gross rate of 10.50 percent raised about 350 billion drachmas and the two-year zeros with a yield to maturity of 10.1 percent raised about 50 billion drachmas, they said.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
